---
// Terms page. Added on 2026-10-17 because OpenAI's plugin directory asks every listing
// for a terms address; the owner's instruction: "refer to MIT license". So the page
// adds no terms of its own to the software: the MIT licence in the repository is the
// licence, and this page explains it in plain words and points to it. What the page
// says about the user's own site and the services they sign up for restates facts from
// the toolkit's docs/WHAT-THE-SKILLS-RUN.md; it creates no new duty. The note in section
// 3 on the imprint and privacy drafts restates the toolkit's own template headers
// (impressum.astro and privacy.astro under skills/new-website/templates/astro/src/pages/:
// "A solid baseline, not legal advice. When in doubt, have it reviewed.").
// Still open, for the owner (not legal advice; have it reviewed when in doubt):
//   1. Whether a liability clause under German law is wanted beside the licence's
//      own "as is" wording. The page adds none.
//   2. Governing law and place of jurisdiction: the page names none.
//   3. A German version, as for /privacy.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import EmailLink from '../components/EmailLink.astro';
import { COMPANY } from '../config';
---
<Base
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="The terms for using Croftweaver: free software under the MIT licence, given as it is, beside the services you choose, each under its own terms."
  image="/images/og/terms.jpg">
  <section class="wrap">
    <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
    <p>
      Last updated: 23 October 2026. This page covers the Croftweaver software (its
      skills, its plugins and its installer) and this website.
    </p>

    <h2>1. The software is free, under the MIT licence</h2>
    <p>
      Croftweaver is published by Daniel Melter as open source under the MIT licence;
      {COMPANY.legalName} runs this website. You may use it, copy it, change
      it, share it and sell work made with it, also for clients and commercially, at no
      cost. The one condition: keep the copyright notice and the licence text in every
      copy of the software or of a substantial part of it.
    </p>
    <p>
      The licence itself is in the repository:
      <a href="https://github.com/karero/croftweaver/blob/main/LICENSE">LICENSE</a>.
      Where this page and the licence differ, the licence applies. A few skills build on
      other people's open-source work; their licences are listed in
      <a href="https://github.com/karero/croftweaver/blob/main/THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md">THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>2. As it is</h2>
    <p>
      The licence gives the software "as is", without warranty of any kind: neither its
      author nor we promise that it suits your purpose or that it has no faults. Read the licence for
      the exact wording.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Your site</h2>
    <p>
      The skills run inside the AI assistant you choose, usually on your own computer.
      Neither we nor the author see what they build or check it before you publish it.
    </p>
    <p>
      That includes the imprint and the privacy page that the skills draft for your
      site. These texts are starting points, not legal advice, and what the law asks of
      you depends on your country and on what your site does. Ask a lawyer to review
      them before you publish, or use your own imprint and privacy texts instead.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Other services have their own terms</h2>
    <p>
      Croftweaver works with services you sign up for yourself, for example GitHub,
      Cloudflare, Google Search Console and the AI assistant you use. Your agreement with
      each of them is your own, under their terms, and any fees go to them. We are not
      part of those agreements. Which services each skill contacts is listed in
      <a href="https://github.com/karero/croftweaver/blob/main/docs/WHAT-THE-SKILLS-RUN.md">What the skills run</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>5. This website</h2>
    <p>
      We write the pages on croftweaver.com with care, but they can be out of date.
      Links to other websites lead to content we do not control. Who runs this website is
      in the <a href="/imprint">imprint</a>; how it handles personal data is in the
      <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Changes and contact</h2>
    <p>
      We update this page when something here changes, and we adjust the date at the top.
      Questions about these terms: write to
      <EmailLink address={COMPANY.email} subject="Terms of Use" />.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
